msg
Trade Record: Scorn?Tindervale Exchange

Filed with the Scorn Trade Hall, Coastal Ledger Annex
Season: Late Ember, Year 417

Parties Involved:

Scorn, via licensed caravans operating under the Eastern Guild Charter

Tindervale, represented by the Fireborne Accord Circle

Goods and Services Exchanged:

From Scorn to Tindervale:

Sheets of reinforced writing glass, heat-tolerant and impurity-free

Glass rods and panes suitable for thermal inscription

Replacement crates for cracked or stress-clouded surfaces

Purpose:
The Fireborne of Tindervale utilize glass as a stable medium upon which controlled flame can inscribe records, diagrams, and memory-traces without degradation. Stone fractures; parchment ignites; metal warps. Glass alone endures prolonged contact with sentient flame.

From Tindervale to Scorn:

Fireborne-assisted excavation services in deep and unstable mine shafts

Controlled heat application for vein exposure and stone separation

Hazard mitigation through fire-guided collapse prevention

Notes:
Fireborne participation has increased ore yield and reduced loss of life in Scornian mining operations, particularly in sulfur-rich and fault-prone strata. No Fireborne injuries were recorded; minor equipment melting was noted and accepted as operational loss.

Special Provisions:

Fireborne workers are not to be extinguished, bound, or enclosed during operations

Mining shifts limited to durations agreed upon to prevent dissipation

All trade glass to be transported unmarked; inscriptions remain property of Tindervale

Record Closed By:
Maris Feld, Trade Clerk of Scorn
Witnessed by three Fireborne signatories, marks heat-sealed into glass

Ledger sealed and archived.
